Research conclusions and limits
title end

paragraph start
Colour research is inconsistent, and a review concluded that general rules are hard to derive from it. So the colour choices are decisions made under uncertainty and are tested on the brand own posts.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Supported: a consistent look aids recognition, red used sparingly pulls attention, vivid colours raise arousal more than pale ones, and low saturation reads as less exciting.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Not supported or not found: white as an accent, purple, monochrome social feeds, and any effect that depends on culture. These stay hypotheses.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Plan: use the palette as designed, record each colour choice as a decision, and run the first experiments from the experiments log before changing anything.
paragraph end

paragraph start
todo: review these conclusions after the first ninety days of results
Replace hypotheses with measured results.
paragraph end

